GREEN V1 every SfxId has one unique cue string and the string maps back to it
GREEN V2 null, empty and unknown cue text map to SfxId::None
GREEN V3 drift: the first 52 SfxIds are the reference catalogue (game/src/core/sfx.ts), in its order
GREEN V3 reference ids are Original; spell-cast..invalid-magic are native hooks; the tone is diagnostic
GREEN V4 every cue literal on an emitting line of native/core maps to an SfxId (closed vocabulary)
GREEN V4 the scan finds all 31 cue ids the core is known to emit (a positive control on the scan)
GREEN M1 drift: MusicContext is music.ts's union, in its order
GREEN M1 drift: song_for_context is music.ts CONTEXT_SONG, row for row (26 rows)
GREEN M1 the 16 songs carry the patch's Files.txt titles
GREEN M2 the location switch matches the driver for every g_location 0x00..0xff
GREEN M2 a frigate (tiles 0x20..0x27) overrides the location; a skiff does not
GREEN M2 combat wins over everything (Engagement), and after VICTORY! the Theme
GREEN M3 hut and village share Greyson's Tale; silence has no song; creation is the Amiga Theme
GREEN S11 a semantic cue reaches the backend once, with its parameter and the SFX gain
GREEN S11 SfxId::None never reaches the backend
GREEN S12 with the supported patch a context reaches the backend as its song
GREEN S12 the same song is never restarted (the driver's cmp al,[0x11e])
GREEN S12 Silence stops the song (selector 0x03)
GREEN S13 without the supported patch no context, at any volume, ever reaches the backend
GREEN S13 a stock install keeps the requested context (no-op) and still plays SFX
GREEN S14 SFX volume changes the SFX channel only (no music gain, no restart)
GREEN S15 music volume changes the music channel only
GREEN S15 and SFX still carry the SFX gain
GREEN S14 re-applying unchanged volumes touches neither channel
GREEN S16 SFX volume 0 is mute: nothing is submitted
GREEN S16 music volume 0 stops the song but remembers the context
GREEN S16 raising the music volume from 0 starts the context's song again
GREEN S17 gain: 0 -> 0, 50 -> 8191, 100 -> 32767 exactly, above 100 clamps, strictly increasing
GREEN S17 applying any gain to any sample never overflows or flips sign; max gain is unity
GREEN S17 a Settings step is 10, clamped at 0 and 100 without wrapping
GREEN S20 a refusing backend is asked once per request -- never retried, never waited on -- and the service degrades to silence
GREEN S20 no backend at all (no audio hardware) is silence, not an error
GREEN S18 a load flushes the old world's SFX and leaves music alone
GREEN S20 audio.cpp holds no loop-until, delay, sleep, wait or RTOS primitive
RED S20 the device backend's game-thread entry posts with a 0 timeout; I2S writes run on its own task
GREEN P1 the committed stock pack (written by the TS packer) is Valid and says stock: no music
